.TITLE "clear"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Clears the terminal screen. It removes all previous output from the __terminal buffer__ and positions the cursor at the top of the window.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**clear**
Clears the entire terminal screen.
> 

**clear -x**
Clears the screen but preserves the scrollback buffer.
> __-x__ preserve scrollback flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __clear__ helps maintain a focused workspace by removing clutter from previous command outputs. On most terminal emulators, the keyboard shortcut __Control + L__ performs a similar action.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/clear.html__
